WEBVTT

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.250
Entry team has seized the facility!

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.250
Verified corpse of suspected terrorist leader!

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.920
Currently removing explosives planted inside.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.110
Three escaped terrorists have seized a plane

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.930
and taken a female Japanese national hostage.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.930
Damn! Poor follow-through.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.430
S-Save me...

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.060
The terrorists have demanded fuel and a pilot.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.060
How's Kazami doing?

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:48.560
Boomerang, how does the situation look?

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.940
Hearing you call me that makes me feel nostalgic, Second Lieutenant.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.700
About twelve degrees left of the control tower's light.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.950
The target's there.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.950
We will now refuel and begin the hostage exchange.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.270
You'll lead.

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.830
Incapacitate the target with your first shot.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.270
Danny's suppression unit
will breach immediately after.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:17.030
It's a two thousand meter shot... in fog, no less.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.510
It's impossible right now.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:22.350
The negotiator can't delay any longer. Do it.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.420
Impossible. Can't be done.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.440
I want to go home.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.200
Wimp. Why don't I switch you out for a while?

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.360
Hey, Kazami!

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.860
The word "impossible" doesn't exist for a soldier!

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.860
There's nothing you can't do!

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.560
I went out of my way to bring your sorry ass all the way from Japan.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.060
Don't drag my name through the mud!

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.710
If I had to drag it through something, it wouldn't be mud, Agnes.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.620
You little bastard! Your mouth's getting as rotten as your master's!

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.580
It was a joke, Captain Garrett.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:52.660
You're awfully easygoing.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.790
Listen up! The hostage takes priority!

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.130
Aye, ma'am!

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.580
Hey, you read me, Boomerang?

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:01.510
Yeah, Robby.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.240
I finished installing the monitoring equipment.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.520
I'm sending the data to your PC.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.250
You've got a bush dog icon, right?

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:09.270
Bush dog?

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:11.700
You mean this?

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.280
Yup! Give that bush dog little-sister-character a click!

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.140
You're sick. Hurry up and seek treatment.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:23.030
If Shimoheihei-chan is activated, I'm sure you know what happens.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.290
Oh, well. I'll give it a try later.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.290
Firing restrictions have been lifted.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.800
I repeat, firing restrictions have been lifted!

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.140
Bang!

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:54.480
Shit!

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:56.750
I didn't hit the hostage, did I?

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:57.980
Impact verified!

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.160
Alpha! Bravo! Charlie!

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.360
Commence infiltration!

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.100
Let's go! Ooh rah!

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.760
Your CheyTac is amazing, Millie.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.550
Well done, Boomerang. How are you holding up?

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:23.920
Horrible. Come get me on the double, and bring a barf bag.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:24.910
I'm gonna throw up.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.890
Sounds like you're fine.
Come back on your own.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.220
What about the hostage?

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:34.880
The criminals packed up and ran for it?!

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.810
What are the airport police doing?

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.700
They escaped by sea?!

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.630
They say you never know

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:47.440
when a bullet you've fired in battle will find its way back to you.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.660
Luckily, perhaps, I'm still alive.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:55.550
I'm grateful that you saved me.

00:03:55.550 --> 00:04:02.340
But I'd like to declare my disapproval now!
Wasn't there a better way?!

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:07.750
Yo, Shorty. What's this girl yelling in Japanese about?

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.100
Sounds like she's upset about her rough rescue.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.850
I was sprayed with blood and pushed into the ocean!

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:17.690
And when I asked you to save me,
you pointed and laughed at me!

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.860
It was awful!

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.360
Hey, Danny, look at this.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.330
This girl has a Showa birth date.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.340
Showa?

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.370
It's a Japanese era. It means...

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:32.090
Huh? You're telling me this girl is older than me?!

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.790
That's how it would work out, yeah.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:37.560
Japanese people really do look young, huh?

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.000
Eddie's niece looks more grown-up than her, and she's fresh out of elementary school.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.520
I think she's a special case.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:48.060
I'm telling you, I'm not a middle schooler!

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.600
I'm older than that! Older than you!

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:54.100
Not to mention, I'm a teacher!

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.350
I'm a principal!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:04:59.610
Your gratitude?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.700
I'm an adult after all.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:06.490
You did save me, so I should thank you accordingly.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.320
And I have the ability to do so.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.620
She probably means more than a gift certificate.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.080
There's really nothing...

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:19.080
Anything is fine. Just ask.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.280
Your gratitude... Gratitude, huh?

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.590
Let's see... School, maybe?

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:37.020
I think I always wanted to try to be an
ordinary student in an ordinary school.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:47.240
Kazami Yuuji Dossier and Personal Record.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.530
Document preparer: Harudera Yuria.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:55.270
She's already familiar with superficial personal records.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:06:01.290
The girl down there wants to know what makes Kazami Yuuji tick.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:07.300
Kazami Yuuji. Family of four: father, mother, sister, and himself.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:09.270
Father: Ryouji.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:12.070
Apparently ran a small antique shop,

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:15.340
but his primary income actually came from an under-the-table business

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:17.960
that acted as a middleman for political donations.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.240
Mother: Satoko.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:21.480
Weak of spirit.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:25.420
Despite mistrusting others' affections, was often reliant upon them.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.400
Thought to have been a sad woman.

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:29.510
Sister: Kazuki.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:34.280
Blessed from early childhood with
prodigious talent for science and the arts,

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.440
she was thought to have a promising future,

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:40.460
but was killed in the Takizono Academy Minibus Disaster.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.670
Details of the incident are in another file.

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:48.350
Two years Kazuki's junior,
Yuuji is the Kazami family's second child.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:50.640
Compared to Kazuki, who was praised as a prodigy,

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.680
Yuuji was ordinary, and was treated harshly by those around him.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:58.430
Kazami Kazuki...

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:04.560
Yuuji's older sister Kazuki's prodigious
talent first manifested at the age of four.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:08.290
The first sign was when she began creating

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:11.950
sketchbook copies of famous artwork stored in her family's home.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:15.950
She could do anything she set her mind to,

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.950
and always produced above-average work.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.800
Blessed with artistic talent among other things,

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:25.960
pieces she painted at age ten are said to now be worth several million yen.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:29.210
Come in.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.850
Kazami-san has arrived.

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.220
Show him in.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:37.860
I read the documents beforehand.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:39.800
You know, nobody writes documents by hand anymore.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:42.320
It's easier to dispose of paper copies.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:45.070
I put all my rough drafts through a shredder.

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:47.840
If you're going to go that far, just incinerate them.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.170
Machines can restore shredded documents now.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:54.140
And it takes a while, but people can do it by hand, too.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:56.740
Who has that much time on their hands?

00:07:57.190 --> 00:08:00.370
So? What did you call me here for?

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:03.590
The documents I submitted should have covered everything.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:07.680
I've got a report to write, too.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.190
I'm going to ask you a few questions now, so please answer.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.380
What do you want to know?

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:15.890
Let's see... For starters, maybe about your sister?

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.600
Does that have anything to do with my promotion?

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:23.470
There are a number of oddities surrounding your sister's death.

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:26.390
That's the official stance.

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:30.530
My true motive is to learn how you felt about your sister.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.860
It's exactly as I wrote in the documents.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:40.660
A long time ago, I went through a phase
where I tried to avoid my too-brilliant sister.

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:46.040
You always go quiet like that.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.670
When things get hard, you can say so, okay?

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:53.050
Things <i>are hard for me...</i>

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:57.120
People treat me like I'm a fool because I'm with you.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:07.730
Hey, Yuuji. Want to play catch?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.370
Why don't you use your left hand?

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.620
Aren't you the one who told me I should use my right?

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:25.010
That's just for chopsticks.

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:28.120
It doesn't really matter which hand you use to throw.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.010
Try throwing with your left hand.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:38.090
See? You're better with your left!

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:42.260
But let's practice so you can throw better with your right hand, too.

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:44.520
Why?

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:48.600
It would be troublesome for you if you
couldn't use your left hand for some reason.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:50.520
Use chopsticks with your right hand, though.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.520
Okay.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.610
Today was fun.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:57.400
Yeah.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:59.410
Hey, Yuuji?

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:03.950
There's nothing you can't do.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.240
It'll just take you longer than me.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:07.910
Really?

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:12.070
Yes. What's important is that you don't give up.

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:16.420
I'm sure someday, not giving up will be your strongest weapon.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.530
No matter how hard the situation is,

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:23.820
even when everyone around you has given up and fallen into despair,

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:27.680
be a man who can stand back up.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:32.610
Listen. Being hardworking is a talent.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:33.820
Understand?

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:34.940
Yeah.

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:40.300
What a nice picture.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:45.340
It's embarrassing.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:47.080
I like this picture.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:50.460
There's nothing embarrassing about it.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.340
Take down that picture!

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:59.720
Kirihara-san is coming to see us!
These childish scribbles are a disgrace!

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.840
I put up this picture because I like it! Don't insult it!

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.720
Yuuji!

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.980
What's this, Yuuji? Are you trying to be spiteful?

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:25.740
I'm sorry, Yuuji.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:32.250
One day, I met a strange man.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:36.630
So, um... What price are you thinking about for my daughter's painting?

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:38.980
Thank you very much!

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:44.220
Who's this young boy?

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:47.140
Kazuki's little brother, Yuuji.

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:49.640
Well, how about that...

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:54.150
Little boy, do you like chocolate?

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:06.030
Does he paint, too?

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:10.410
Don't be absurd. He isn't blessed with that sort of talent,

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.410
I'm embarrassed to say.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:18.960
Why can't you paint like before?!

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:21.210
You used to make more paintings!

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:25.500
That's because I was a child.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:33.730
Nee-chan, you can actually paint better than you used to, so why'd you lie?

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:38.730
Being known as "the girl who can
do anything" is annoying. Besides...

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:44.990
Manga?

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:47.710
I borrowed them from a girl in my class.

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:50.200
Once I'm done reading them I'll lend them to you.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.940
But he'll get mad again and say you'll turn into an idiot.

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:55.290
Listen, Yuuji.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.410
If you read manga,

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:59.750
then you'll have something to talk about with other kids who like it.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:03.340
That's a very important thing.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:06.190
Friends who've met through a shared hobby

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:08.860
are more precious than you might think.

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:13.270
Are friends really that important?

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:14.890
They are.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:18.590
People who become adults without realizing
the importance of interpersonal connections,

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:22.310
realize they have no one there when it matters most,

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:23.630
and fall into despair.

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:29.200
Take a good look at our father.
Do you want to become a man like him?

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.850
I don't know.

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:33.240
Never mind.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:37.380
If you've finished your homework,
go outside and play with your friends.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.580
I don't have any friends, though.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:42.640
In that case, work hard to make some.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:48.390
My sister, who learned to "lower her level" in order

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:51.380
to live like a normal person, canceled her plans to study in Paris,

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:54.080
and maintained a relatively quiet lifestyle.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.020
Even then, the paintings my sister would sometimes make

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:00.870
became the sole source of income for our household,

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:04.900
and no one in our home could defy her.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:10.410
On the other hand, my parents treated me very harshly.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.910
My parents and sister ate out a lot while trying to influence potential buyers,

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.410
but I always stayed home alone.

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:22.060
I'm home.

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:23.670
Yuuji?

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.510
Yuuji...?! What are you eating?

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:32.700
Bread.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:36.520
You're dunking bread in water...

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.360
Was I not supposed to eat it?

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.000
Here! Look, Yuuji!

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.900
There's plenty of food in the fridge!

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:49.370
But nobody told me it's okay to eat it.

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:51.500
If I eat that without permission, I'll get scolded.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:53.130
Nobody will scold you!

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:56.910
If anyone scolded you for something like that, I'd scold <i>them!</i>

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:00.320
What have I done?

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:06.170
I'm eating out, and I didn't even notice my little brother was eating something so meager.

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:08.530
I'm sorry, Nee-chan...

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:11.960
You haven't done anything wrong.

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:14.710
I'm sorry I never noticed.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:20.260
That night I heard my sister give my parents a stern talking-to

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:22.350
until it was very late.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:25.360
But of course, nothing improved.

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:30.610
My father despised me more and more, and didn't even hide it anymore.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:34.990
As for my mother, she openly started to avoid me,

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:37.220
as if to say, "Wise men steer clear of danger."

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:42.290
But she never forgot to give me my daily bread.

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:47.250
You're late, Yuuji.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:49.760
I was playing with my friend.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:54.260
I see, that's nice. Don't tell me your friend is a girl?

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:55.660
She is...

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:57.140
Who? Where's she from?

00:15:57.140 --> 00:16:01.880
Um, her name's Sachi. I don't know where she lives.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.290
Bring this girl home with you next time.

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:11.280
No way. Nee-chan, you always tease my friends when I do that.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:17.700
How rude. I'm judging whether your friends are fit for you or not.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:21.470
Aren't you the one who told me to make some friends?

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:24.580
I don't remember telling you to make <i>female friends.</i>

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:27.360
Why are they always girls?

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:30.090
Is my jealousy that amusing to you?

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.000
You know, Nee-chan—

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.220
I mean, I do get it.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:37.310
Your face is like mine, you're adorable like a girl,

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:39.920
you're quiet and hate roughhousing,

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:43.850
and you're surprisingly good at sports,
despite how soft you look.

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:46.170
And most of all, you're kind.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:50.360
I'm sure you're quite popular, but I don't like it.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:53.100
I don't like it at all!

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:58.120
If you want female friends that badly, then get my permission first!

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:03.040
You're forbidden from befriending girls I haven't approved of!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.500
Got it?

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.500
Okay, Nee-chan.

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:13.800
Don't make that face, Yuuji.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:18.760
Someday I'll definitely find an appropriate girl for you,

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:24.770
so be careful you don't become a man who makes girls cry in the meantime.

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:26.540
I'll be careful.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:30.240
Hey! You aren't careful at all!

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:34.300
In fact, it's shocking how close you turned out to what she predicted!

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:37.700
Hey. Don't interrupt me at awkward times.

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:41.450
But... You know? I mean...

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:44.620
So then, regarding this, here...

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:47.960
Practical jokes by your sister?
What did you mean by that, specifically?

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:51.960
I have to explain that, too?

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:55.720
Yuuji, shall we take our bath?

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:57.480
Yeah.

00:17:57.480 --> 00:18:00.220
I called it "practical jokes"...

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:05.260
But siblings bathing together isn't really that unusual.

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:07.390
There were a few others in my class who did it, too.

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:19.240
I went into the bath with my sister, and she washed me.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:20.850
That's all there was to it.

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:25.900
Nee-chan?

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:29.780
This is something all close siblings do.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:36.640
Hey, have you ever kissed someone, Yuuji?

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:39.060
You kiss me all the time, Nee-chan.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:41.240
That's not what I meant.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:44.010
You know, like in that manga we read together,

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:47.350
where two adults kiss when they love each other.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.990
Have you ever done that?

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:50.100
I haven't.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.440
Want to try it, then?

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:53.960
With me.

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:54.930
Why?

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.410
Because <i>I want to try it!</i>

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:21.720
Hey, Yuuji. Do you know what "incest" is?

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.420
What's that?

00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:25.710
It's when siblings love each other.

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:26.810
I see.

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:30.300
But that's pretty normal, isn't it?

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:35.030
There's nothing odd about siblings
loving each other, don't you think?

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:36.190
You're right.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:41.500
You love me, don't you, Yuuji?

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:42.200
Yeah.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:44.200
Right?

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:47.130
I love you, too.

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:49.610
But siblings can't get married.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.710
I think that's a much stranger thing.

00:19:56.640 --> 00:19:59.740
Why can't siblings get married?

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:03.970
Well, there are issues with genetics, and some other things...

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:06.310
Am I so drawn to you, my little brother,

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:11.420
because it's right, down to my genes,

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:14.850
or have my genes perhaps begun to go haywire?

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:19.380
Either way, these feelings of mine are right.

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:21.110
I don't really get it...

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:24.030
In the first place, what's so abnormal about it?

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:26.670
Is it abnormal for siblings to kiss?

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:28.930
What about hugging each other, like this?

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:30.680
I don't know.

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:36.060
Hey, Yuuji. Answer me. Am I abnormal?

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:38.880
Nee-chan, you're always right.

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:42.350
Thank you, Yuuji.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:47.320
I learned all kinds of things from my sister.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:52.920
Eventually, my sister enrolled at a famous private academy,

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:56.560
and betrayed our parents' expectations by not joining a fine arts club.

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:59.970
She joined the basketball club instead.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:09.070
She hid her prodigious talent and spent her days peacefully.

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:13.390
There were times when she put her genius to work,

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:15.460
and manipulated those around her like pawns.

00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:21.460
No, they most likely never realized they were put into motion by my sister.

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:25.470
I was the only one who knew the truth about my sister.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:29.900
Even our parents moved according to her will.

00:21:29.900 --> 00:21:33.490
From the bottom of my heart, I was afraid of that side of her.

00:21:33.490 --> 00:21:38.350
"This person definitely isn't human. She might even be a God."

00:21:39.100 --> 00:21:42.860
I feared her, yet I depended on her.

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:48.220
I thought that lifestyle would never end.

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:50.660
Yes, until that day...

00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:55.100
The discovery of the minibus,

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:59.790
at the bottom of a deep ravine,
was reported two weeks after the incident.

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:02.220
There was only one survivor.

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:04.800
Evidence of several people fighting

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:07.370
was discovered at the site.

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:11.800
My sister's death was confirmed mid-September.

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:16.320
My father, who had pinned his hopes on my sister, fell into depression

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:17.310
and alcoholism.

00:22:19.020 --> 00:22:23.920
Before long, he began to abuse my
mother and me practically every day.

00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:27.940
Hide in here.

00:22:27.940 --> 00:22:30.700
Don't come out until I say it's okay.

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:36.330
We're out of booze!

00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:39.110
I told you over and over not to let it run out!

00:22:38.700 --> 00:22:43.590
My mother just kept saying, "I'm sorry, I'm sorry."

00:22:39.110 --> 00:22:40.270
I'm sorry.

00:22:40.270 --> 00:22:43.590
You think "sorry" is gonna cut it?!

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:46.580
My mother was a very weak person.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:47.590
I'm sorry...

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:52.930
There wasn't a single good thing about living with that man.

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:55.350
My mother decided we should leave.

00:23:04.590 --> 00:23:07.740
Starting today, this is our new home.

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:14.300
This is all there is. I'm sorry.

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:17.620
It's delicious.

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:22.790
It wasn't really comfortable, but my father wasn't there.

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:25.130
That alone made it feel like heaven.

00:23:27.270 --> 00:23:31.540
I'll do my best until you grow up, Yuuji.

00:23:31.540 --> 00:23:33.510
You don't have to worry about a thing.

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:38.710
Mother worked day and night to support me.

00:23:40.820 --> 00:23:45.400
Our lives carried on like that for a year. Then, one day...

00:23:55.850 --> 00:23:58.540
Did you think you could run away from me?

00:23:59.690 --> 00:24:01.790
Go buy some booze, Yuuji!

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:03.900
No!

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:09.170
You're the goose that lays the golden eggs.

00:24:09.170 --> 00:24:11.580
I'll make you give me another genius!

00:24:11.580 --> 00:24:13.630
And then once again, I'll...

00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:17.130
Yuuji! Don't come over here!

00:24:17.130 --> 00:24:19.450
Did you buy the booze?!

00:24:19.450 --> 00:24:20.560
Yeah.

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:22.360
Leave it over there and get out!

00:24:23.580 --> 00:24:25.740
Stop it, Dad.

00:24:25.740 --> 00:24:27.730
Shut up! Wanna get hit?!

00:24:27.730 --> 00:24:31.360
Leave, Yuuji! I'll be fine!

00:24:31.360 --> 00:24:32.740
What?!

00:24:32.740 --> 00:24:35.700
Don't go actin' like you're a real mother!

00:24:40.360 --> 00:24:42.370
Stop it! Let Mom go!

00:24:44.360 --> 00:24:46.460
You little shit!

00:25:06.320 --> 00:25:07.350
I'll kill him!

00:25:09.360 --> 00:25:13.180
Stand and fight. Nothing will change if you keep running away.

00:25:13.180 --> 00:25:16.360
So no matter how painful and unrelenting life gets...

00:25:17.230 --> 00:25:20.560
Hold chopsticks and write with your right hand,

00:25:20.560 --> 00:25:24.160
and when you throw a ball or stand in the batter's box, use your left.

00:25:24.870 --> 00:25:28.760
So, which hand will you use to kill a man?

00:25:41.720 --> 00:25:43.270
Mom, are you okay?

00:25:43.270 --> 00:25:45.040
Let's run!

00:25:45.040 --> 00:25:46.720
Yuu-chan.

00:25:47.990 --> 00:25:51.270
You're right. We'll have to run away again.

00:25:51.270 --> 00:25:55.120
But I wonder, how far away should we run?

00:25:55.120 --> 00:25:58.030
How long will we have to keep running?

00:25:58.510 --> 00:25:59.790
Mom...

00:25:59.790 --> 00:26:04.220
I'm sorry. You're fast, Yuu-chan, so you run away right now.

00:26:04.220 --> 00:26:08.000
Go on ahead of me. I'll follow you later.

00:26:15.340 --> 00:26:17.930
This is everything we have.

00:26:19.150 --> 00:26:22.620
Keep a good hold on it, so you don't lose it.

00:26:23.660 --> 00:26:26.120
Go on, hurry and run.

00:26:26.120 --> 00:26:26.930
Where?

00:26:27.320 --> 00:26:30.720
Let's see, how about the station for now?

00:26:30.720 --> 00:26:32.310
Yuu-chan, can you get there on your own?

00:26:32.310 --> 00:26:33.360
Yeah.

00:26:33.360 --> 00:26:37.620
Good! Do your best on your own, then.

00:26:37.620 --> 00:26:40.320
Go on, get going.

00:27:04.180 --> 00:27:05.970
Hacked up with a kitchen knife...

00:27:05.970 --> 00:27:07.420
There was a suicide note.

00:27:07.420 --> 00:27:08.840
A murder-suicide, apparently.

00:27:20.680 --> 00:27:22.240
Hey! You can't go inside!

00:27:42.230 --> 00:27:43.760
Hey! You all right?!

00:27:43.760 --> 00:27:45.270
Hold it together!

00:27:54.620 --> 00:27:58.210
I killed my father, and drove my mother to suicide.

00:28:03.500 --> 00:28:06.530
I wonder why things turned out this way?

00:28:07.280 --> 00:28:09.540
Where did I go wrong?

00:28:10.620 --> 00:28:12.820
I'm sorry, Yuu-chan.

00:28:14.900 --> 00:28:16.190
I'm sorry.

00:28:21.010 --> 00:28:24.820
When I was discharged from the hospital, I was taken in by a man named

00:28:24.820 --> 00:28:26.380
Kirihara Rei.

00:28:26.380 --> 00:28:29.820
An art dealer and a customer of my father.

00:28:31.740 --> 00:28:34.060
Congrats on being discharged, Yuuji-kun.

00:28:34.560 --> 00:28:38.050
You don't have to worry about anything anymore.

00:28:43.100 --> 00:28:45.860
That really suits you, Yuuji!

00:28:47.930 --> 00:28:50.080
Silent as ever, aren't you?

00:28:51.520 --> 00:28:55.960
Well, it's because you're like this that I've taken an interest in you.

00:28:56.990 --> 00:28:59.780
Children can't live on their own.

00:28:59.780 --> 00:29:02.960
I had plenty of food, shelter from the wind and rain,

00:29:03.740 --> 00:29:07.220
and, ignoring that they were for girls, enough clothes.

00:29:08.720 --> 00:29:10.720
There were no issues whatsoever.

00:29:27.240 --> 00:29:30.000
He won't be back for a while.

00:29:37.340 --> 00:29:39.500
Don't speak of this to anyone.

00:30:02.820 --> 00:30:04.480
Did you kill him?

00:30:09.740 --> 00:30:11.740
Not bad, Yuuji!

00:30:11.740 --> 00:30:13.940
You're amusing!

00:30:13.940 --> 00:30:17.250
That's fine, Yuuji. You're exactly right.

00:30:17.850 --> 00:30:22.220
That's exactly the kind of instinct the future of mankind should possess!

00:30:24.460 --> 00:30:25.510
You're not mad?

00:30:25.510 --> 00:30:29.260
Oh, my. It's been a while since I heard your voice.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:34.090
Has killing a man healed your broken heart a little?

00:30:35.320 --> 00:30:37.810
Come here, Yuuji. I'll give you some chocolate.

00:30:42.420 --> 00:30:45.220
It's okay. I'm not mad.

00:30:45.220 --> 00:30:48.620
I hated that man, too.

00:30:48.620 --> 00:30:51.160
In fact, let me praise you for a job well done!

00:30:52.460 --> 00:30:55.540
All right, Yuuji. Let's study some more.

00:30:55.540 --> 00:30:58.790
I'm sure you'll become a tool more excellent than any other.

00:30:59.440 --> 00:31:01.420
An excellent tool?

00:31:01.420 --> 00:31:06.670
Or would you prefer to continue living here as a pet?

00:31:07.760 --> 00:31:08.670
I do not know.

00:31:09.070 --> 00:31:13.680
Your life is such that there's no telling
whether you're alive or dead, anyway.

00:31:14.400 --> 00:31:18.220
Think of it as repaying a favor and do your best.

00:31:23.510 --> 00:31:25.990
I remember that it was a cold country.

00:31:26.760 --> 00:31:30.340
In that country, Kirihara was called "Heath Oslo,"

00:31:30.340 --> 00:31:32.380
and I was ordered to call him that, too.

00:31:33.740 --> 00:31:38.700
There, Oslo had established a vocational school.

00:31:39.570 --> 00:31:40.830
It was a school in name only.

00:31:41.470 --> 00:31:46.800
In reality, it was nothing more than a terrorist training camp Oslo had organized.

00:31:51.300 --> 00:31:53.050
Is school fun?

00:31:52.580 --> 00:31:54.550
Heath Oslo took a liking to me,

00:31:53.050 --> 00:31:54.550
Yes. It's fun.

00:31:55.150 --> 00:31:59.060
so no one there particularly liked me.

00:32:00.660 --> 00:32:04.060
Among the many things we trained in,
I had a talent for marksmanship,

00:32:04.750 --> 00:32:08.010
particularly at long range.

00:32:09.660 --> 00:32:12.200
That made the others dislike me even more.

00:32:18.560 --> 00:32:22.420
Harassment under the pretense of training never ended.

00:32:26.820 --> 00:32:28.340
Are you okay?

00:32:32.580 --> 00:32:35.550
I had no previous recollection of that girl.

00:32:36.210 --> 00:32:39.010
If I remember right, her name was something like "Marlin."

00:32:39.900 --> 00:32:43.890
She treated me whenever I got hurt,
and if my chance to eat was taken away,

00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:48.020
she would save her food and share it with me.

00:32:48.900 --> 00:32:51.180
The world wasn't all that bad, after all.

00:32:52.510 --> 00:32:56.160
On occasion, I would be instructed by Oslo himself.

00:32:56.850 --> 00:33:01.230
Ready, Yuuji? Don't depend on an unrefined tool like a gun.

00:33:01.230 --> 00:33:02.910
It's gotta be <i>blades</i>.

00:33:03.840 --> 00:33:08.590
It's kill or be killed, so kill them before they kill you.

00:33:11.340 --> 00:33:13.840
If you go outside, it's nothing but enemies.

00:33:15.460 --> 00:33:19.860
Even your family were your enemies, so you must understand, right?

00:33:22.820 --> 00:33:25.520
I'm your only ally.

00:33:25.520 --> 00:33:28.230
Except for me, everyone's an enemy.

00:33:28.230 --> 00:33:30.990
Survive and make it back to me.

00:33:32.310 --> 00:33:33.610
Very good, Yuuji!

00:33:34.160 --> 00:33:38.240
I'm truly grateful that I knew your shitty dad.

00:33:38.240 --> 00:33:41.240
Kazami Yuuji, you're the greatest!

00:33:45.930 --> 00:33:49.430
I was given my final test, said to be my graduation exam.

00:33:50.790 --> 00:33:53.340
I'd pass if I killed or incapacitated my opponent.

00:33:53.340 --> 00:33:55.380
It was an easily understood rule.

00:33:56.020 --> 00:33:58.130
And, my opponent was...

00:34:00.470 --> 00:34:01.640
Marlin.

00:34:08.480 --> 00:34:11.820
You killed your own kin with those hands.

00:34:11.820 --> 00:34:14.150
This is nothing in comparison, right?

00:34:38.770 --> 00:34:43.390
"Sorry, Marlin," I apologized in my head.

00:34:54.740 --> 00:34:56.610
What am I doing?

00:34:57.490 --> 00:35:00.360
At this rate, I'll be just like my dad!

00:35:03.490 --> 00:35:04.570
What's wrong?!

00:35:04.570 --> 00:35:05.370
Kill her!

00:35:05.370 --> 00:35:10.710
Kill her! Kill her! Kill her! Kill her!

00:35:30.650 --> 00:35:32.770
This is my sin.

00:35:33.650 --> 00:35:35.770
My sin of hurting a woman...

00:35:35.770 --> 00:35:37.530
What's wrong, Yuuji?!

00:35:37.530 --> 00:35:39.280
Didn't you murder your own father?!

00:35:39.650 --> 00:35:41.910
No matter how many people you kill, it's all the same!

00:35:41.910 --> 00:35:44.030
Stand up! Stand and fight!

00:35:51.750 --> 00:35:53.710
Unbelievable.

00:35:54.060 --> 00:35:57.590
I swear, Yuuji, what will I do with you?

00:36:11.130 --> 00:36:13.730
I'm so sorry.

00:36:14.430 --> 00:36:16.950
I wonder why things turned out this way.

00:36:18.390 --> 00:36:20.700
I didn't want to hear those words.

00:36:21.410 --> 00:36:23.740
They were the same words my mother left in her suicide note.

00:36:24.520 --> 00:36:28.740
They were pessimistic words that left me feeling weak and powerless.

00:36:31.310 --> 00:36:33.750
How are you feeling? Think you can eat something?

00:36:34.360 --> 00:36:35.630
I don't want anything.

00:36:36.040 --> 00:36:39.500
If you don't eat something, your injuries won't heal.

00:36:41.180 --> 00:36:45.010
Why did that man take you in?

00:36:48.850 --> 00:36:52.640
You know, I'm going to graduate from this place soon.

00:36:54.440 --> 00:36:55.520
That's great.

00:36:56.030 --> 00:36:56.880
Yeah.

00:36:58.040 --> 00:37:00.270
If you're worried about me, don't be.

00:37:00.270 --> 00:37:04.780
Once you leave this place, you're better off
forgetting me and everything that happened here.

00:37:05.610 --> 00:37:08.580
I'm bad at fighting.

00:37:09.210 --> 00:37:14.580
If I could live without hurting others, that would be best.

00:37:18.500 --> 00:37:20.060
Well, I'll come again.

00:37:25.710 --> 00:37:29.700
Marlin said that as she walked out.
She never came to see me again.

00:37:30.360 --> 00:37:32.850
She graduated and left.

00:37:33.580 --> 00:37:37.850
Her final words were meant to tell me she
would come see me again if she survived.

00:37:38.640 --> 00:37:40.860
I've finally come to understand that.

00:37:41.560 --> 00:37:43.990
Oh, that girl died.

00:37:43.990 --> 00:37:46.990
She made a stupid mistake on her first job.

00:37:46.990 --> 00:37:50.400
She'd had some great results, so we expected a lot from her, too.

00:37:50.400 --> 00:37:52.490
Marlin died?

00:37:53.540 --> 00:37:56.710
If I had passed my final exam and graduated,

00:37:56.710 --> 00:37:59.750
would Marlin not have died?

00:38:00.130 --> 00:38:03.000
Those thoughts gave me mixed feelings.

00:38:04.200 --> 00:38:07.420
Because you were kind to someone like me...

00:38:10.200 --> 00:38:14.290
After two months, I was given the chance to graduate again.

00:38:15.160 --> 00:38:17.020
My task was an actual assassination.

00:38:18.040 --> 00:38:20.270
An actual, real-life deployment.

00:38:24.830 --> 00:38:25.530
This is...

00:38:26.320 --> 00:38:28.290
Take it and go.

00:38:28.290 --> 00:38:30.220
For doing nothing?

00:38:30.220 --> 00:38:34.360
You brewed tea for me. That's enough.

00:38:34.360 --> 00:38:36.290
Thank you very much.

00:38:44.280 --> 00:38:46.460
It was a simple job.

00:38:46.460 --> 00:38:48.490
I was the one in charge of that.

00:38:48.490 --> 00:38:52.220
I was a member of an American intelligence agency back then.

00:38:52.640 --> 00:38:57.600
I know. At the time, the CIA called me ET-01:

00:38:57.600 --> 00:39:00.080
"Enfant Terrible #1."

00:39:00.080 --> 00:39:01.730
I heard about it from Asako.

00:39:02.080 --> 00:39:07.490
I had just made Second Lieutenant.
The assignment given to me was to investigate ET-01.

00:39:08.070 --> 00:39:11.360
Yes, you really were a mysterious boy.

00:39:11.970 --> 00:39:16.150
Glenn MacPherson, a judge from the
International Court of Justice, age fifty-seven.

00:39:16.150 --> 00:39:18.370
Stabbed to death in his private hotel room.

00:39:19.210 --> 00:39:24.140
Harold Bowman, CEO of the American bank ABM, age fifty-six.

00:39:24.140 --> 00:39:27.880
Died instantly from a broken neck.

00:39:28.510 --> 00:39:31.430
Benoit Robert, French left-wing radical

00:39:31.430 --> 00:39:34.390
and National Assembly member, age forty-eight. Strangled.

00:39:34.970 --> 00:39:39.000
Paul Graham, freelance journalist, age thirty-eight.

00:39:39.000 --> 00:39:42.070
Died in a car accident on his way home from covering a story.

00:39:42.070 --> 00:39:44.150
Doubts surround the cause of his death.

00:39:44.910 --> 00:39:50.400
We were unable to uncover your identity throughout our investigations.

00:39:50.880 --> 00:39:54.280
But that changed on the night when our all-new test operation, CIAS,

00:39:54.670 --> 00:39:59.280
infiltrated Heath Oslo's residence and found you

00:40:14.800 --> 00:40:19.970
Now, then. I guess it's time I settle our
score from that time with the baby mill.

00:40:54.860 --> 00:40:55.510
Clear.

00:40:56.430 --> 00:40:57.310
And Oslo?

00:40:57.310 --> 00:40:58.310
Still searching.

00:40:58.850 --> 00:41:02.060
Don't let a single one of them escape! Exterminate them all!

00:41:03.570 --> 00:41:05.850
Our perimeter should be perfect.

00:41:26.910 --> 00:41:30.420
Damn it. We can kill these pawns
all day and it won't mean anything.

00:41:31.250 --> 00:41:33.040
Underground passage found in E Block!

00:41:55.450 --> 00:41:56.460
A child?

00:42:04.450 --> 00:42:06.460
Good morning, young lady.

00:42:07.710 --> 00:42:08.540
Huh?

00:42:11.750 --> 00:42:13.740
You're a boy?

00:43:50.150 --> 00:43:51.010
Where is he?

00:44:00.220 --> 00:44:02.860
It's just like you guessed, JB.

00:44:02.860 --> 00:44:06.370
We found something interesting in the basement.

00:44:15.500 --> 00:44:18.030
Yuuji, I've done something regrettable...

00:44:18.890 --> 00:44:20.430
But we'll meet again.

00:44:24.160 --> 00:44:28.640
If I hadn't met Asako that day,
I'm sure I wouldn't be here right now.

00:44:28.640 --> 00:44:30.890
Yes. Nor would you have met me.

00:44:30.890 --> 00:44:34.780
And after that... You probably know better than I do.

00:44:34.780 --> 00:44:37.470
My memories of that time are still fuzzy.

00:44:37.470 --> 00:44:41.010
Drug-induced memory loss, deterioration of consciousness...

00:44:41.010 --> 00:44:42.900
It was the toughest time of your life.

00:44:42.900 --> 00:44:44.410
Well, then.

00:44:44.770 --> 00:44:46.880
Everything up to this point is as I've told you.

00:44:46.880 --> 00:44:48.430
Do I need to continue?

00:44:48.430 --> 00:44:51.660
Of course. I'll listen until you reach the present day.

00:44:54.490 --> 00:44:57.170
In that case, let me take a breather.

00:44:57.910 --> 00:45:01.610
Stop, Shark Man! Don't involve humans in this battle!

00:45:01.610 --> 00:45:05.970
Who cares? I'll do whatever I want!

00:45:05.970 --> 00:45:09.680
Ignorant fool! If you don't understand words, then eat my fatty tuna!

00:45:09.680 --> 00:45:10.810
Tuna! Tuna! Tuna!

00:45:11.180 --> 00:45:13.180
Shark Fin Cutter!

00:45:13.180 --> 00:45:15.670
Wh-What?! My fatty tuna was negated?!

00:45:15.670 --> 00:45:17.700
Oh, no! Tuna Man's in a pinch!

00:45:17.700 --> 00:45:20.130
Stand up! Stand up, Tuna Man!

00:45:20.130 --> 00:45:21.650
Shark Man...

00:45:23.230 --> 00:45:26.450
Come to think of it, where's Yuuji?
I don't think I've seen him since this morning.

00:45:26.450 --> 00:45:30.950
Oh, what, just 'cause you haven't seen him in a little while you feel lonely?

00:45:30.950 --> 00:45:34.320
N-Not really! I just wondered where he went!

00:45:34.320 --> 00:45:37.460
Th-That's all! Don't get the wrong idea!

00:45:37.460 --> 00:45:40.080
Please calm down, Michiru-sama.

00:45:40.080 --> 00:45:43.410
Please learn from Sakaki-san, who's used to being alone.

00:45:43.410 --> 00:45:45.810
Huh?! I'm not used to being alone!

00:45:45.810 --> 00:45:47.450
In the first place, I'm not alone!

00:45:47.450 --> 00:45:49.800
So? Where did Yuuji go, anyway?

00:45:49.800 --> 00:45:52.780
He said he was going to Ichigaya for work.

00:45:52.780 --> 00:45:54.600
Think he's up to somethin' again?

00:45:55.070 --> 00:45:58.480
He mentioned he was taking a promotion exam soon.

00:45:58.480 --> 00:46:03.070
Ah, so that's what he's been spendin' his sweet time in his room for.

00:46:03.070 --> 00:46:06.680
By the way, Komine-san, what's that you've been holding all this time?

00:46:07.680 --> 00:46:08.440
Oh, yes.

00:46:08.440 --> 00:46:11.660
I, Komine Sachi, wondered if I couldn't be of use to Kazami-san,

00:46:11.660 --> 00:46:15.580
since he's so busy with work, and was cleaning his room for him.

00:46:16.020 --> 00:46:18.920
Did you find crusty, stiff underwear or anything?

00:46:19.420 --> 00:46:22.420
No, it was something even more outrageous.

00:46:24.980 --> 00:46:28.690
A personal report of Kazami Yuuji's past?

00:46:28.690 --> 00:46:29.430
Yes.

00:46:29.900 --> 00:46:33.640
Restored from scraps of paper after it was put through a shredder.

00:46:33.640 --> 00:46:35.430
Are you incredible or just an idiot?

00:46:35.430 --> 00:46:38.350
We shouldn't look at that without permission, should we?

00:46:38.350 --> 00:46:39.750
Is that so?

00:46:39.750 --> 00:46:43.260
As I was restoring it, I inadvertently looked over it,

00:46:43.260 --> 00:46:46.440
and stole a glance at Kazami-san's heroic past.

00:46:46.950 --> 00:46:49.250
I couldn't bear my guilty conscience,

00:46:49.250 --> 00:46:51.450
so I brought it here to acquire accomplices.

00:46:51.890 --> 00:46:55.690
One for all, all for one.

00:46:55.690 --> 00:46:57.200
Great words, are they not?

00:46:57.200 --> 00:46:59.080
No way, we can't!

00:46:59.470 --> 00:47:01.250
If you have no interest,

00:47:01.250 --> 00:47:04.850
I'll shred it again, and incinerate the remains.

00:47:05.830 --> 00:47:08.830
Oh, no, that's... Right?

00:47:11.060 --> 00:47:13.720
Could you not look to me for approval?

00:47:14.270 --> 00:47:18.730
Come to think of it, we hardly know anything about Yuuji's past.

00:47:18.730 --> 00:47:21.730
I haven't heard any details, either.

00:47:23.730 --> 00:47:26.480
Well, then. What shall we do, everyone?

00:47:37.320 --> 00:47:40.980
Next time: "The Cocoon of Caprice I."
